<title>USA: Times Mirror expands stock buyback.</title>
<headline>Times Mirror expands stock buyback.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Times Mirror Co said it extended its ongoing share repurchase program by authorizing the buyback of an additional 12 million common shares.</p>
<p>It said the repurchases are expected to be made over the next three years on the open market or in private transcations.</p>
<p>The latest buyback plans will be added to the program authorized in 1995 for a repurchase of up to 12 million shares. Of that original program, about 70 percent have been repurchased.</p>
